Message-ID: <77971833-7A99-41D2-AEB1-E9136C04C9CE@research.att.com>

Gunnar,

it is evident from your report that rJava actually installs properly.


On Sep 7, 2006, at 4:28 PM, Gunnar Hellmund wrote:

> I have tried to install JGR on R 2.3.1 on Ubuntu (Dapper Drake)  
> (using both sun-java versions from repositories and a 'manual  
> installation' of Sun-Java 1.5)
> [...]
>> library(rJava)
> Error in dyn.load(x, as.logical(local), as.logical(now)) :
>        unable to load shared library
> '/usr/local/lib/R/site-library/rJava/libs/rJava.so':
>  libjvm.so: cannot open shared object file: No such file or directory
> Error in library(rJava) : .First.lib failed for 'rJava'
>

Your R was not compiled with Java support. You have two ways to fix  
this - either re-compile R with Java support or set LD_LIBRARY_PATH  
to reflect your Java library path.

Given your previous output, something like this may work:

export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/lib/jvm/java-1.5.0-sun-1.5.0.06/jre/lib/ 
i386/client:/usr/lib/jvm/java-1.5.0-sun-1.5.0.06/jre/lib/i386:/usr/ 
lib/jvm/java-1.5.0-sun-1.5.0.06/jre/../lib/i386

Cheers,
Simon


