Message-ID: <C3FDEDD6-5BEA-4543-8762-97E02454BDD1@research.att.com>


On Sep 14, 2006, at 6:22 PM, Paul Shannon wrote:

> I depend upon (and much admire) rJava in my Bioconductor package  
> 'gaggle'.
>
> When I run "R CMD check ~/tmp/gaggle_1.1.7.tar.gz" I get an error.   
> The
> error appears to be caused by the absence of a NAMESPACE file in  
> rJava_0.4-9.tar.gz:
>
>   * checking R files for non-ASCII characters ... OK
>   * checking whether the package can be loaded ... ERROR
>   Loading required package: rJava
>   Loading required package: graph
>   Error: package 'rJava' does not have a name space
>   Error: package/namespace load failed for 'gaggle'
>   Execution halted
>
> May I request that, when convenient, you add a NAMESPACE file to  
> the rJava package?
>

You may (and you're not the first one ;)), but unfortunately it is  
currently not trivial to do, because rJava uses its package  
environment to cache certain Java objects and they cannot be created  
until .jinit is called, so they cannot be sealed in a namespace  
(there are some other minor technicalities as well - object  
prototypes and some functions have a similar problem - they need to  
be modified after the namespace is loaded, so using an extra  
environment won't solve it, either). However, I'll definitely look  
into that...

@Kurt, is there a way for a package with a namespace to depend on  
rJava without the above error?

Thanks,
Simon


