^^-- you have a Java version mismatch - you will need Java 1.5 to run  
those classes, but you have only Java 1.4.

Now, I'm not sure why the classes are in 1.5 format. Please make sure  
you install the correct packages ("JGR","iplots","rJava","JavaGD")  
from CRAN. I have checked, and the current CRAN packages all use JDK  
1.4 classes, so I have no idea where you got the 1.5 classes from. If  
you have trouble installing from CRAN, you can try the nightly builds  
from http://rosuda.org/R/nightly/, but the CRAN version is known to  
work.

If you still have only 1.5 classes (don't ask me why), updating your  
Java should fix the problem. Unfortunately, updating Java will cause  
R Java configuration to be out of date, so you'll need either to  
reconfigure R again or edit $R_HOME/etc/ldpaths to contain the  
correct path. Perhaps you may as well want to compile R 2.4.0 beta  
while you're at it, because it's very close to the release and it has  
a nice script "R CMD javarecheck" that configures Java anytime.

