> (b) "Note: For all systems you need Java 1.5 or higher!"
>

The issue was with JRI which was not enforcing 1.4 compatibility.  
This was fixed in rJava_0.4-10, so it can be now removed - save for  
the issue below ;).


> But: Java 1.5 isn't available for Max OS X 10.3 (Apple's policy  
> tricks), so either (a) or (b) is invalid.
>
> I also read in the "Problem running JGR" thread, that actually JGR  
> may not necessarily need Java 1.5 but may work with 1.4.
>

It appears that you are being bitten by exactly this. After some  
digging I have finally found the problem - there was one class in  
iplots that has not been compiled with Java 1.4 flags, because it was  
compiled in the distribution script separately to include the current  
version number. Please install iplots as follows:

install.packages("iplots",,"http://rosuda.org/R/nightly",type="source")

and let me know if that works for you. I'll push the corresponding  
changes to CRAN if that works as desired.

Thanks,
Simon


>
> Logdata:
>
> Here is the R output:
> > library("JGR")
> Lade nÃ¶tiges Paket: rJava
> Lade nÃ¶tiges Paket: JavaGD
> Lade nÃ¶tiges Paket: iplots
> NewObject("org/rosuda/iplots/Framework","()V",...) failed
> Exception in thread "main" java.lang.UnsupportedClassVersionError:  
> org/rosuda/ibase/Common (Unsupported major.minor version 49.0)

^^ 1.5 (=49.0) required, but not supported (1.4=48.0).





