On Sep 28, 2006, at 2:44 PM, Jarrett Byrnes wrote:

> My apologies.  I had thought one could run iplots from within R  
> natively (i.e. I was running library(iplots))
>

You can do so everywhere except for Mac OS X. The reason has to do  
with the Apple's Java implementation (R is not thread-safe and  
Apple's Java cannot be run on the main thread, probably due to event  
loop issues in Cocoa). Admittedly this fact is not well documented -  
I'll try to fix that.

Cheers,
Simon


